# Normalize text files to LF in the repository and in checkouts on every
# platform, Windows included.
#
# Without this, tools that rewrite line endings (notably black on Windows,
# and some editors) silently convert files to CRLF, which turns a small
# logical change into a whole-file diff. During Phase 1 of the Godot
# compatibility matrix track, a single black run inflated a 264-line
# change into 2651 insertions and 2526 deletions of pure line-ending
# noise. Pinning eol=lf makes the index authoritative: git normalizes on
# `git add`, so the working tree may be CRLF but the diff stays truthful.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets. `text=auto` already auto-detects these, but naming them
# explicitly removes any dependence on that heuristic.
*.ttf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.whl binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
